0..78 Comment "// A theory\'s rule is a cell conversion decides, and a model witnesses it as a"
79..102 Comment "// path in its carrier."
103..105 Comment "//"
106..184 Comment "// A `Path` is a cell a program carries. A model owes one `Path` component per"
185..261 Comment "// rule, between the rule\'s two sides read in its carrier. Where the carrier"
262..338 Comment "// converts the two sides, `here` witnesses the rule. Where it does not, the"
339..417 Comment "// model writes the path. The presented type is the initial model, where every"
418..439 Comment "// witness is `here`."
440..442 Comment "//"
443..520 Comment "// Two models of one left unit law over the naturals show both witnesses. The"
521..593 Comment "// one joining on the left argument converts the law\'s sides, and `here`"
594..671 Comment "// witnesses it. The one joining on the right argument leaves them apart, and"
672..701 Comment "// an induction witnesses it."
702..704 Comment "//"
705..780 Comment "// - see: `model-ascription.gandr` — a rule `here` witnesses at each case"
781..843 Comment "// - see: `model-laws.gandr` — a law stated as its path type"
